##  [Synopsis](https://docs.ansible.com/ansible/2.9/modules/junos_l2_interfaces_module.html#id1)[¶](https://docs.ansible.com/ansible/2.9/modules/junos_l2_interfaces_module.html#synopsis "Permalink to this headline")
  * This module provides declarative management of a Layer-2 interface on Juniper JUNOS devices.


##  [Requirements](https://docs.ansible.com/ansible/2.9/modules/junos_l2_interfaces_module.html#id2)[¶](https://docs.ansible.com/ansible/2.9/modules/junos_l2_interfaces_module.html#requirements "Permalink to this headline")
The below requirements are needed on the host that executes this module.
  * ncclient (>=v0.6.4)


##  [Parameters](https://docs.ansible.com/ansible/2.9/modules/junos_l2_interfaces_module.html#id3)[¶](https://docs.ansible.com/ansible/2.9/modules/junos_l2_interfaces_module.html#parameters "Permalink to this headline")
Parameter | Choices/Defaults | Comments  
---|---|---  
**config** list / elements=dictionary |  A dictionary of Layer-2 interface options  
**access** dictionary |  Configure the interface as a Layer 2 access mode.  
**vlan** string |  Configure the access VLAN ID.  
**enhanced_layer** boolean | 
**Choices:**
  * no
  * yes

|  True if your device has Enhanced Layer 2 Software (ELS). If the l2 configuration is under `interface-mode` the value is True else if the l2 configuration is under `port-mode` value is False  
**name** string / required |  Full name of interface, e.g. ge-0/0/1.  
**trunk** dictionary |  Configure the interface as a Layer 2 trunk mode.  
**allowed_vlans** list |  List of VLANs to be configured in trunk port. It's used as the VLAN range to ADD or REMOVE from the trunk.  
**native_vlan** string |  Native VLAN to be configured in trunk port. It is used as the trunk native VLAN ID.  
**unit** integer |  Logical interface number. Value of `unit` should be of type integer.  
**state** string | 
**Choices:**
  * **merged** ←
  * replaced
  * overridden
  * deleted

|  The state of the configuration after module completion  
##  [Notes](https://docs.ansible.com/ansible/2.9/modules/junos_l2_interfaces_module.html#id4)[¶](https://docs.ansible.com/ansible/2.9/modules/junos_l2_interfaces_module.html#notes "Permalink to this headline")
Note
  * This module requires the netconf system service be enabled on the remote device being managed.
  * Tested against vSRX JUNOS version 18.4R1.
  * This module works with connection `netconf`. See [the Junos OS Platform Options](https://docs.ansible.com/ansible/2.9/network/user_guide/platform_junos.html).


