##  [Synopsis](https://docs.ansible.com/ansible/2.9/modules/junos_vlans_module.html#id1)[¶](https://docs.ansible.com/ansible/2.9/modules/junos_vlans_module.html#synopsis "Permalink to this headline")
  * This module creates and manages VLAN configurations on Junos OS.


##  [Requirements](https://docs.ansible.com/ansible/2.9/modules/junos_vlans_module.html#id2)[¶](https://docs.ansible.com/ansible/2.9/modules/junos_vlans_module.html#requirements "Permalink to this headline")
The below requirements are needed on the host that executes this module.
  * ncclient (>=v0.6.4)


##  [Parameters](https://docs.ansible.com/ansible/2.9/modules/junos_vlans_module.html#id3)[¶](https://docs.ansible.com/ansible/2.9/modules/junos_vlans_module.html#parameters "Permalink to this headline")
Parameter | Choices/Defaults | Comments  
---|---|---  
**config** list / elements=dictionary |  A dictionary of Vlan options  
**description** string |  Text description of VLANs  
**name** string / required |  Name of VLAN.  
**vlan_id** integer / required |  IEEE 802.1q VLAN identifier for VLAN (1..4094).  
**state** string | 
**Choices:**
  * **merged** ←
  * replaced
  * overridden
  * deleted

|  The state of the configuration after module completion.  
##  [Notes](https://docs.ansible.com/ansible/2.9/modules/junos_vlans_module.html#id4)[¶](https://docs.ansible.com/ansible/2.9/modules/junos_vlans_module.html#notes "Permalink to this headline")
Note
  * This module requires the netconf system service be enabled on the remote device being managed
  * Tested against Junos OS 18.4R1
  * This module works with connection `netconf`. See [the Junos OS Platform Options](https://docs.ansible.com/ansible/2.9/network/user_guide/platform_junos.html).


##  [Examples](https://docs.ansible.com/ansible/2.9/modules/junos_vlans_module.html#id5)[¶](https://docs.ansible.com/ansible/2.9/modules/junos_vlans_module.html#examples "Permalink to this headline")
```
# Using merged
#############

# Before State
# ------------
#
# admin# show vlans
# vlan-2 {
#     vlan-id 2;
# }
# vlan-3 {
#     vlan-id 3;
# }

- name: Merge JUNOS vlan
  junos_vlans:
    config:
      - name: vlan-1
        vlan-id: 1
  state: merged

# After State
# -----------
#
# admin# show vlans
# vlan-1 {
#     vlan-id 1;
# }
# vlan-2 {
#     vlan-id 2;
# }
# vlan-3 {
#     vlan-id 3;
# }


# Using replaced
################

# Before State
# ------------
#
# admin# show vlans
# vlan-1 {
#     vlan-id 1;
# }
# vlan-2 {
#     vlan-id 2;
# }
# vlan-3 {
#     vlan-id 3;
# }

- name: Replace JUNOS vlan
  junos_vlans:
    config:
      - name: vlan-1
        vlan-id: 10
      - name: vlan-3
        vlan-id: 30
  state: replaced

# After State
# -----------
#
# admin# show vlans
# vlan-1 {
#     vlan-id 10;
# }
# vlan-2 {
#     vlan-id 2;
# }
# vlan-3 {
#     vlan-id 30;
# }


# Using overridden
##################

# Before State
# ------------
#
# admin# show vlans
# vlan-1 {
#     vlan-id 1;
# }
# vlan-2 {
#     vlan-id 2;
# }
# vlan-3 {
#     vlan-id 3;
# }

- name: Override JUNOS vlan
  junos_vlans:
    config:
      - name: vlan-4
        vlan-id: 100
      - name: vlan-2
        vlan-id: 200
  state: overridden

# After State
# -----------
#
# admin# show vlans
# vlan-2 {
#     vlan-id 200;
# }
# vlan-4 {
#     vlan-id 100;
# }


#Using deleted
##############

# Before State
# ------------
#
# admin# show vlans
# vlan-1 {
#     vlan-id 1;
# }
# vlan-2 {
#     vlan-id 2;
# }
# vlan-3 {
#     vlan-id 3;
# }

- name: Delete JUNOS vlan
  junos_vlans:
    config:
      - name: vlan-1
  state: deleted

# After State
# -----------
#
# admin# show vlans
# vlan-2 {
#     vlan-id 2;
# }
# vlan-3 {
#     vlan-id 3;
# }

```

